          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="svn-tool-ui svn-files" aria-hidden="true"><i>.txt</i><i>.md</i><i>.srt</i></span>
            <b>Save or copy</b><span>As plain text, Markdown with times, or subtitles.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="svn-tool-ui svn-again" aria-hidden="true">Transcribe again</span>
            <b>Transcribe again</b><span>Redo a meeting from its saved audio with a newer model. Cancel puts the old text back.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <aside class="svn-card svn-card--os" aria-labelledby="svn-os-title">
        <h3 id="svn-os-title" class="svn-os-h">Where it records the other side</h3>
        <ul class="svn-os">
          <li><b>Windows</b><span>Records both sides.</span></li>
          <li><b>macOS 13 or later</b><span>Records both sides once you allow Screen &amp; System Audio Recording. On macOS 12 it records your side only.</span></li>
          <li><b>Linux</b><span>Records both sides with PulseAudio or PipeWire.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="svn-os-note">If it can't record the computer's sound, it tells you before you start and keeps your side.</p>
        <p class="svn-consent">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" /><path d="M12 8v5M12 16.5v.5" /></svg>
          <span><b>Let people know you're recording.</b> In many places everyone on a call has to agree to it. The app reminds you the first time.</span>
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <!-- companion: Transcribe a file -->
    <article class="svn-file">
      <div class="svn-file-copy">
        <p class="svn-file-k">Also new: Transcribe</p>
